/*
 * NON-HUMAN-GENERATED SOURCE
 * This source file was generated by AI and was not human-generated.
 *
 * Usage:
 * 1. Add DVO_TrafficSimulator to a GameObject and assign a vehicle prefab whose
 *    root contains DVO_Vehicle. Every spawned vehicle receives Init().
 * 2. Add paths in the inspector. Select and drag keypoints in the Scene view;
 *    Shift-click the XZ plane to append points and mark selected points as stops.
 * 3. Set the deterministic seed, prewarm time, duration, spawn settings, and the
 *    two avoidance radii. The slowdown radius must be at least the forced radius.
 * 4. Click Bake Traffic, then use Play/Pause Preview or the preview-time slider.
 * 5. At runtime call UpdateSimulation(double time), or drive UpdateState through
 *    the existing DVObject/Simulated-X timeline integration.
 *
 * Assumptions:
 * - Paths are one-way, open polylines with at least two keypoints.
 * - Motion and simulation state use XZ only; globalY is presentation only.
 * - Prefab renderers define preview bounds and prefab pivots are center-bottom.
 * - Each stop-sign keypoint is serviced once per vehicle.
 * - Avoidance radii are per-vehicle radii, so pair distances use their diameters.
 */

